    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d303-a1">

                <pb facs="0352" n="252" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg252"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure—Translation]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Mexican Acting Secretary for Foreign Affairs</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Medina</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        American Chargé</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Summerlin</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-01-30"><hi rendition="#italic">January 30,
                        1920</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 50</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Chargé d’Affaires</hi>: The Government of the
                    United Mexican States, in view of private reports on the personality of Mr.
                    William O. Jenkins, rendered by the authorities of the State of Puebla, finds
                    itself in the painful necessity of stating to you that it is not possible for it
                    to issue to him the Exequatur as Consular Agent of the United States of America
                    in the city of Puebla, as requested by that Embassy in Note number 272, dated
                    March 18, 1918.</p>
                <p>I must also inform you that, by direction of the President of the Republic, the
                    provisional authorization issued by the Mexican Government under date of March
                    12, last year, to Mr. Jenkins, to perform provisionally the duties assigned to
                    him, is no longer in effect.</p>
                <p>In view of the foregoing, I take the liberty of returning to you the Commission
                    of the said Mr. Williams O. Jenkins.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. Medina</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
